---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';

const email = site.contact.email;
const updated = '27 October 2026';
const cookies = [
  { name: '_clck', who: 'This site (set by Clarity)', purpose: 'Remembers a random Clarity ID for your browser, so visits can be counted' },
  { name: '_clsk', who: 'This site (set by Clarity)', purpose: 'Links the pages of one visit into a single session recording' },
  { name: 'CLID', who: 'Microsoft (clarity.ms)', purpose: 'Notes when Clarity first saw this browser on any site using Clarity' },
  { name: 'MUID', who: 'Microsoft', purpose: 'Identifies browsers visiting Microsoft sites (used by Microsoft for analytics and operations)' },
  { name: 'ANONCHK, MR, SM', who: 'Microsoft', purpose: 'Technical cookies that manage and synchronise the MUID cookie' },
];
---

<Base title="Privacy & cookies" description="How this site handles your data and cookies." bodyClass="is-gallery-page">
  <main id="main" class="page legal">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="tag">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy &amp; cookies</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose legal-prose">
      <p>
        This is a personal photography portfolio. It has no accounts, forms, shop or advertising. The only optional data
        collection is usage analytics, which runs only if you agree to it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        Bryce de Bruyn is responsible for this website and for the personal data described here. Contact:
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What is collected and why</h2>

      <h3>1. Hosting</h3>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, run by GitHub, Inc. (United States). Like any web server, GitHub receives
        technical information when you load a page, such as your IP address, browser and the page requested, and may
        keep it in server logs for security and to run the service. This is needed to deliver the site (legal basis:
        legitimate interest, GDPR art. 6(1)(f)). See
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>2. Analytics: Microsoft Clarity (only if you accept)</h3>
      <p>
        If you click <strong>Accept</strong> on the analytics banner, the site loads Microsoft Clarity to understand how
        people use it, so I can improve it. Clarity records how you interact with the pages: mouse movements, clicks,
        scrolling, the pages you view, how they render, and information about your device and browser. It produces
        heatmaps and session recordings. Clarity always masks anything typed into input boxes (this site has none).
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> your consent (GDPR art. 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw it at any time, as easily as you gave it.</li>
        <li><strong>If you click Decline</strong> (or do nothing), Clarity is not loaded at all and sets no cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>Who processes it:</strong> Microsoft. For visitors in the EU, Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, which may transfer data to Microsoft Corporation in the United States under the European Commission's standard contractual clauses. Data is stored in Microsoft's Azure cloud.</li>
        <li><strong>How long:</strong> according to Microsoft, recordings are kept for 30 days (some selected recordings up to 9 months) and heatmaps for up to 9 months.</li>
        <li>More: <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Microsoft privacy statement</a> and <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/clarity/setup-and-installation/cookie-list" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Clarity's cookie list</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3. Emails you send me</h3>
      <p>
        If you email me, I receive your email address and message in my email account (Gmail, provided by Google) and
        use them only to reply to you. I keep them only as long as needed for our conversation.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
      <p>These cookies are set <strong>only after you click Accept</strong>:</p>
      <div class="legal-table-wrap">
        <table class="legal-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Cookie</th><th scope="col">Set by</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {cookies.map((c) => (
              <tr><td class="mono">{c.name}</td><td>{c.who}</td><td>{c.purpose}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Microsoft decides how long its cookies last; see Clarity's cookie list for details.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site also saves one small item in your browser's local storage, <span class="mono">bdb-analytics-consent</span>,
        which simply remembers whether you accepted or declined analytics, so the banner doesn't appear on every page. It is
        kept for 6 months, after which you are asked again. Because it only stores your choice, it doesn't require consent.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything else the site needs, including fonts, photos and the live ISS orbit data, is served from this site
        itself, so your browser doesn't contact other companies unless you accept analytics or follow an external link
        (YouTube, LinkedIn).
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can change your analytics choice at any time:
        <button class="text-btn" type="button" data-consent-open>open cookie settings</button>. Choosing Decline after
        accepting stops Clarity, which also deletes its cookie for this site. You can also block or delete cookies in your
        browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR you have the right to access, correct or delete your personal data, to restrict or object to its
        processing, to data portability, and to withdraw consent at any time. To use these rights, email
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. Clarity data is pseudonymous (it isn't linked to your name), so I may need
        details such as the date and time of your visit to find it.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you think your data has been handled improperly, you can complain to the Spanish data protection authority,
        the <a href="https://www.aepd.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Agencia Española de Protección de Datos (AEPD)</a>,
        or to the authority in your own country.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this site starts collecting anything new, this page will be updated and the date at the top will change.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
